1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,580
I kicked a pebble and let it fly far away.

3
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:29,420
Talking with the head of the gym class,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for
staying so full of energy.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some
good spirits somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
there's only winning.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, and the unchanging townscape

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are calling,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Stuffing yakitori in my mouth,

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,840
just looking at it...

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:57,500
of the acorn-cap hat,

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:04,080
the sun sets from the
waterworks toward Ōishi.

15
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,100
Tomorrow, too,
it'll end with something dropped.

16
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,660
Katsushika, happiness lost for a while,

17
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,300
because I'm just a guy
who only just noticed.

18
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:27,080
Memories of the food stalls.

19
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:38,500
How do I look?

20
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,840
Reiko, it suits you!

21
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:46,740
Mm-hmm.

22
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:48,220
Chief.

23
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,160
Is this all right?

24
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:55,060
Does something look wrong?

25
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,160
No, Nakagawa, that's a bit...

26
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:03,060
Kei-chan, a man's kimono sash
should be tied lower down.

27
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:06,180
But I did exactly what my senpai told me to.

28
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,820
Speaking of festivals,

29
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,940
I don't see Ryo-san,
who always rushes over first.

30
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:15,740
Ryo-chan went to pick up Lemon-chan.

31
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:16,860
Sorry to keep you waiting!

32
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,220
Oof, there we go.

33
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:21,860
How cute.

34
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:24,060
It really suits you!

35
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:24,860
Do you think so?

36
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:27,340
That's the Edokko spirit, that is.

37
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,300
Is that so?

38
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:31,020
It's crowded, so don't get separated.

39
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:31,620
Yeah.

40
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,800
Alright, let's go! Off we go!

41
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,260
If we don't hurry, we'll miss the mikoshi.

42
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:38,460
Wait up, Ryo-chan!

43
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:39,660
I'm heading out.

44
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:43,720
Even on your day off,
be careful about sticks and fights.

45
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:44,460
Yes.

46
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,260
Eeeeeeh!

47
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:00,960
Heave-ho!

48
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,100
Heave-ho!

49
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:03,420
Heave-ho!

50
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:03,440
Heave-ho!

51
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:14,900
Not bad, right? Ryo-chan, you're itching to carry it too, aren't you?
No, today I'm on lemon duty, right?

52
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:19,540
Whatever you say,
it's obvious you're holding yourself back.

53
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,980
Kankichi!

54
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,020
What is it?

55
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:26,620
That big drum, Lemon!
I wanna give it a whack!

56
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,420
You think so? Alright, leave it to me!

57
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:32,300
Hey! Let me hit it too!

58
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:35,740
Ryo-san, go ahead! Don't hold back!

59
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:37,620
Alright, here we go, Lemon.

60
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:45,160
Don't hold back,
just hit it with all your might.

61
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:45,740
Yeah!

62
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,700
That's it, that's it, keep it up!

63
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,560
The rhythm is perfect.

64
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,420
You're putting grown adults to shame.

65
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,680
Goldfish scooping

66
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,840
Yeah, that's it.

67
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,160
I'll go get a lemon goldfish for you.

68
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,200
And then a doll from
the shooting gallery too.

69
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,840
Senpai, you're really in the mood!

70
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:12,180
Here goes. Goldfish scooping takes spirit!

71
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:13,800
Toriet

72
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,700
Toriet

73
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,980
What a haul! How about that!

74
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:27,520
Give me a break, you'll bankrupt me!

75
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,220
Alright, I'm on a roll!

76
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:35,840
Don't underestimate an
active police officer!

77
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:49,480
Heh, I give up!

78
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:51,380
Hehehe~

79
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,180
Sorry!

80
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,060
Alright, this is it!

81
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:04,640
Eek!

82
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:05,660
Whoa!

83
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,160
Hahaha, what a haul, what a haul!

84
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,600
I feel like I'm forgetting something...

85
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,280
Oh no! Damn it! How could I let this happen!

86
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:16,920
Lemon!

87
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,040
Hey! Lemon!

88
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:22,460
Where is she? Lemon! Lemon!

89
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,240
What's wrong, senior?

90
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:27,320
What do you mean what's wrong?
Did you see Lemon?

91
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:30,580
Lemon-chan was watching the candy sculptures intently,
you know.

92
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:33,000
I saw her at the cotton candy stall.

93
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,000
I see!

94
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:40,040
Lemon!

95
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:41,600
Found him!

96
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:43,420
Lemon!

97
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,720
Wait, it's not him.

98
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,560
Mama!

99
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:47,740
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

100
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:48,460
Hey, sorry about that.

101
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:50,500
Did I startle you? Wrong person.

102
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,580
Could it be, Kan-chan?

103
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,280
It's me, Miharu.

104
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:58,660
Miharu-chan?

105
00:05:58,660 --> 00:06:01,100
Weren't you running a night
stall with Otome-baasan?

106
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,340
Yes, it's been a long time.

107
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:04,200
Never expected to meet like this.

108
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:04,540
Mama.

109
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:25,760
Finally, it's over!

110
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:29,380
Hey, Kankichi!

111
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:32,220
You came to school dressed for the festival?

112
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:35,420
Well, once class is over, we're free.

113
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:37,140
Straight to the shrine from here.

114
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,160
Here we go.

115
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,960
We're starting the children's mikoshi now!

116
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:51,080
Everyone, gather!

117
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,020
Yes!

118
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,620
Hurry, hurry!
We've got to get the best spot!

119
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:58,140
Yeah.

120
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:04,600
Yatta, we're first!

121
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:06,540
We're first too!

122
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:07,300
Says who?

123
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,900
Bunta and Kanemei from the next town.

124
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:12,860
A trio of little brats

125
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,020
What are you talking about?

126
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:21,400
That's right! Together the three of us add up to a perfect 100 points,
everyone knows it!

127
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:26,080
What did you say?
Your trio only adds up to 60 points!

128
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,540
How do you know that?

129
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:31,240
I just guessed, you idiot!

130
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,960
Whoever calls someone an idiot is the idiot!

131
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:34,640
Hey, you two!
What do you think you're doing?

132
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,800
I won't let fighters carry the mikoshi!

133
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,860
Uh-oh, it's that bearded gorilla!

134
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:42,760
Alright, let's settle this with the mikoshi!

135
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,180
Yeah!

136
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:45,480
Let's go!

137
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:49,380
Washoi! Washoi! Washoi! Washoi!

138
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:53,440
You did it now! Come on, bring it on!

139
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:08,880
Ajii! Ajii!

140
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:37,900


141
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:56,280


142
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,680
You should just put that away, that thing.

143
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:08,900
That's strange, there are always yakisoba and okonomiyaki stalls there.
I wonder if something happened to Miharu's grandma.

144
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:13,720
Her house should be right behind this shrine, I'm sure.
Let's go check it out

145
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,060
No, Grandma, you have to stay in bed!

146
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:30,540
When I hear that festival music,
my body just starts moving on its own.

147
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:33,220
The doctor said you shouldn't move around.

148
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:35,460
It's fine, just a little bit.

149
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:38,180
Come on, it's just a sprain.

150
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:39,520
Grandma.

151
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,220
Hey, what's going on?

152
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:46,020
Let me go.

153
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,320
I absolutely have to open my stall.

154
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,320
Even if you say that,
you can't with that leg.

155
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:55,580
Whether it's possible or not,
I have to open the stall.

156
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:59,480
Otherwise, they might stop
finding me a spot from next time on.

157
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:02,380
That bearded gorilla is saying that?

158
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:06,960
He's the one who runs everything at the festivals around here,
from assigning the spots on down.

159
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:11,300
Since they've found us a spot,
we have to properly open the stall.

160
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,980
No, that's just how we do things.

161
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:16,580
I see.

162
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:21,180
Alright, we'll do it for you.

163
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:23,080
Anyone can do it if they try.

164
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:25,960
We just have to open the
stall like we promised, right?

165
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:27,700
Yeah, let's do it.

166
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,260
Yeah, yeah.

167
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,560
I'll help too.

168
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:34,140
Hey, Grandma, just relax and rest easy.

169
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,720
You lot.

170
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:42,460
Once you take this on,
I won't allow any half-hearted work.

171
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:46,140
I'm counting on you for today's
good Miya and tomorrow's main Miya.

172
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:47,860
Leave it to us!

173
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:51,900
Thank you, Gan-chan,
Ton-chan, Chinkichi-kun.

174
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,840
Alright, preparations are set.

175
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,560
The propane's ready too.

176
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,400
Then let's get the cooking prep started.

177
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:12,040
First, the flour and
vegetables for the okonomiyaki,

178
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:16,260
Miharu, could you get the containers
and disposable chopsticks ready?

179
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:17,180
Got it.

180
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:22,620
Here goes.

181
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:24,540
Toppe, light the fire.

182
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:25,740
We'll start with the yakisoba.

183
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:27,820
Chinkichin, fan it with the paper fan!

184
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:30,200
We'll draw in customers
with the tasty smell.

185
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,140
Okay.

186
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:34,380
Alright.

187
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,300
Here we go!

188
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,280
The flame's too strong!

189
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,240
The water keeps coming!

190
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,700
No, water's no good!

191
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:49,740
Water's no good.

192
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,540
Even Mount Akagi ends tonight.

193
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:04,800
and now I must part ways with you,
my beloved underlings.

194
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:14,500
Kankichi!

195
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,620
The okonomiyaki's turned into monja!

196
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:18,580
I made it too runny.

197
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,600
Alright, at least the flour -

198
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,500
We somehow managed to make it work!

199
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,400
Right, now it starts.

200
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:39,100
Welcome!

201
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:41,040
It's the samba group.

202
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:44,440
Why are you two doing something like this?

203
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:47,640
Who cares, there's a reason for it.

204
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:51,700
Don't know what's going on,
but this stall's a real dump.

205
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:52,360
Kan-chan.

206
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,380
Shut up, you're in the way. Just go home.

207
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,800
What's your problem?
We were about to buy something!

208
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,740
That's right, we're customers!

209
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:03,080
After all, the customer is king, right?

210
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:05,080
For a flower goddess, you

211
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,280
Did you say something?

212
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,320
No, nothing at all.

213
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:11,960
That's three servings of yakisoba.
We'll throw in a little extra as a service.

214
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:18,320
Here you are, sorry for the wait.

215
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,360
You did it, Kankichi!

216
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,100
Nice!

217
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:33,840
Serves you right!

218
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:37,020
It's our special yakisoba with
chili peppers and prepared mustard.

219
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,500
Hey, you lot!

220
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:41,620
What do you think you're doing?

221
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,080
Bearded gorilla!

222
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:57,360
This is supposed to be Granny Tome's spot.

223
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:59,080
What on earth is going on?

224
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,100
That's right, that's right.

225
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,240
Who gave you permission to open a stall?

226
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,760
K-Kankichi!

227
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:04,780
Kan-chan!

228
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:09,360
Granny Tome put me in charge,
so I'm helping run the stall.

229
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:10,900
What?

230
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,680
Stop talking nonsense.

231
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,580
It's not nonsense, you idiot!

232
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,840
This brat is defying
Beard Gorilla's big brother!

233
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,880
Leave out the "Beard Gorilla" part!

234
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:23,000
S-sorry, Beard... I mean, Taxi big brother!

235
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:25,000
What should we do? Shall we drive them off?

236
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:25,720
Yeah.

237
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:31,903
Sure enough,

238
00:14:31,953 --> 00:14:35,440
that looks like Tome's
granddaughter over there, but

239
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:40,320
since her grandma sprained
her leg and can't run the stall,

240
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:43,460
we're running the stall in her place.

241
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:48,560
She said if she doesn't,
they won't find her a spot next time.

242
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:52,440
Who wouldn't be? There are fifty thousand
other people who want to run a stall.

243
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:58,340
Fifty thousand? More like sixty, seventy, eighty thousand.
Eighty thousand, at least.

244
00:14:58,340 --> 00:14:59,460
Nice one.

245
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:05,720
That doesn't mean we can't run
the stall in grandma's place, right?

246
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:08,660
These brats always have
a comeback for everything!

247
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:12,685
We get your point. But listen,

248
00:15:12,735 --> 00:15:15,420
this isn't for kids. It's not a game.

249
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,900
We're not doing this for fun.

250
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:22,060
No matter what you say,
we're not moving from here.

251
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:23,900
Me too.

252
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:25,500
Me neither.

253
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,140
B-boss.

254
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,660
For a brat, you've got some nerve.

255
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:40,081
Well, I'll let it slide for today,

256
00:15:40,131 --> 00:15:43,520
but if you cause any trouble,
you'd better be ready!

257
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,360
Tch...

258
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,760
I nearly pissed my pants.

259
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:55,660
Thanks, Kan-chan, Ton-chan, Chinkichi-kun.

260
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:59,920
Please, that bearded gorilla
didn't scare us one bit.

261
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:03,000
Kan-chan!

262
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:07,260
I'm fine, I'm fine,
I just let my guard down.

263
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:07,900
Yeah, yeah.

264
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:10,440
Shut up, you were scared too!

265
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:30,780
You really worked hard, thank you.

266
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:33,040
I thought it would be easier than this.

267
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,120
We kept messing up at first, too.

268
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:38,320
Hey, for a first time, we did pretty well.

269
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:39,820
Yeah, right.

270
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:42,900
Tomorrow's the main festival day,
so we'll do our best from the morning.

271
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,760
Grandma, you can rest easy now.

272
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:59,000
The rain and wind have really picked up,
haven't they?

273
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:09,520
Typhoon No. 18, which had been
moving north across the Pacific,

274
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:14,060
is expected to pass through the Kanto region
from late tonight until early tomorrow morning.

275
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:18,120
In areas along its path,
both rain and wind will grow stronger,

276
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,940
so please stay fully alert.

277
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:21,920
Oh no, a typhoon is coming!

278
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:24,580
If that happens,
what's going to happen to the stall?

279
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:27,960
It's old and pretty shaky, after all.

280
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:34,760
We're going to protect it ourselves.

281
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,080
Are you serious, Kankichi?

282
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:40,100
What if the typhoon blows the stall away?

283
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,340
Then we won't be able to
run the business anymore.

284
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:43,320
Stop it.

285
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,960
Why, Grandma?

286
00:17:46,380 --> 00:17:48,180
You don't have to go that far.

287
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,360
Your feelings are enough.

288
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:56,260
But... but...

289
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:02,380
You've been running this business since long ago,
risking everything, haven't you?

290
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:09,300
I'm doing it.

291
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:10,600
I'll do whatever I can.

292
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:13,200
I hate just sitting around doing nothing.

293
00:18:13,780 --> 00:18:14,520
Pan-chan!

294
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:16,020
Me too.

295
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:16,940
Me too.

296
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:17,900
Big brother.

297
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:28,560
Just follow me and you'll be fine.

298
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:29,200
Let's go!

299
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:34,580
What about the stall?

300
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,860
Good, it's still okay!

301
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:41,780
But we have to do something fast,
or it'll get blown away!

302
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,160
But what are we going to do?

303
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:46,520
That's right! There were those
shime leaves we use for dashi, right?

304
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:47,800
Go get those!

305
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:53,180
Yes!

306
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:57,600
We'll tie the stall to the ginkgo
tree with these shime leaves!

307
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:17,200
Mm, right.

308
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,600
Eeeeeeh!

309
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,200
Okay, that should hold for a while.

310
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:41,540
We just have to endure until morning.
We can't fall asleep.

311
00:19:43,220 --> 00:19:43,580
Yeah.

312
00:19:44,020 --> 00:19:45,380
No way we're letting it blow away!

313
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:47,640
That's right, it's our stall after all.

314
00:19:53,920 --> 00:20:13,640
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu!

315
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:16,280
We can't protect all the
vegetables by ourselves either,

316
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,420
so what are we supposed to do?

317
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:29,400
Damn it!

318
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,600
What do we do?

319
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:40,460
Who's there? What are you doing?

320
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,680
You guys

321
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:45,680
Higu... gorilla...

322
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:53,060
If the stalls get blown away,
we won't be able to hold the festival.

323
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:57,020
Gather up all the rope
and tie the stalls together.

324
00:20:57,540 --> 00:20:59,240
Round up as many young men as you can!

325
00:20:59,340 --> 00:20:59,620
Yes, sir!

326
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:01,220
And another thing...

327
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:01,860
Hehe.

328
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:03,460
Take off your raincoats.

329
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:05,440
Yes, sir!

330
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:08,880
Eh...

331
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:11,000
I guess I've gained
some respect for you two.

332
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:12,740
Come on, do your best!

333
00:21:14,860 --> 00:21:17,280
The festival's still on tomorrow.

334
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:19,820
Yeah.

335
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:44,940
Hey?

336
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:51,040
Grandma, Miharu.

337
00:21:51,580 --> 00:21:55,380
You did a great job. Thank you.

338
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,180
We did it, didn't we?

339
00:22:01,180 --> 00:22:03,400
Yeah, we worked hard.

340
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:08,080
Look, it's starting! Hurry!

341
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:10,320
What are you doing?

342
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:15,760
Yeah, there were times like that,
weren't there.

343
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:18,820
Kan-chan was so manly back then.

344
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:22,240
Well, I never think ahead, so...

345
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:24,860
Whoops, I can't die now!

346
00:22:24,860 --> 00:22:29,100
See you. I'm always at the police box,
so come visit sometimes.

347
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:30,520
Bye-bye!

348
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:37,000
Lemon, lemon

349
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,660
Kankichi

350
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:42,020
Kankichi, there you are!
We've been looking all over for you!

351
00:22:42,020 --> 00:22:43,720
Seriously, Ryo-chan.

352
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:46,140
It was so crowded,
it was really rough going.

353
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:48,920
You were looking for us? That's my line!

354
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:50,640
You really are a handful.

355
00:22:51,460 --> 00:22:53,760
No, that's why I'm the one who...

356
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:56,780
But it was fun, the festival!

357
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:59,320
I see. Here we go.

358
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:10,020
Kan-chan's kid

359
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:11,260
They're the spitting image.

360
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:15,520
Honestly, the way he's acting,
he really looks like Ryo-chan's kid.

361
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:16,720
They really do.

362
00:23:18,420 --> 00:23:19,260
Alright, lemon.

363
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:21,480
Over there,
you can make your own cotton candy.

364
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,500
Shall we go check it out?

365
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,180
Really, Kankichi?

366
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:26,060
Alright, let's go!

367
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:26,700
Yeah.

368
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:53,080
Game, worn-out Coco, guy chari suigyo

369
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:04,700
Always sandals,
always scandal, don't mind it

370
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:05,480
don't mind it

371
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:08,500
Playing cool every day

372
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:09,140
every day

373
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:14,000
Crumpled up the blueprints into
a reprimand and tossed it away

374
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:18,540
Naked instinct, bare instinct, going crazy

375
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:19,500
going crazy

376
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:22,340
Poor or not, so what's the harm

377
00:24:23,820 --> 00:24:28,140
My way, doing it as I please, that's all

378
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:32,680
The stiff chief's thunder,
smoke from his head

379
00:24:33,500 --> 00:24:36,120
Run away and you'll climb the walls

380
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:37,440
Well, how auspicious

381
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,900
In the flowering Edo

382
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:42,040
Ryozan typhoon

383
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:45,480
Raging wildly

384
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:47,580
Working-man play, nine times over

385
00:24:49,580 --> 00:24:51,360
This water runs out,
shell-picking water fish,

386
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:54,600
suigyo batsu, gungyo batsu, Guuraibatsu

387
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:56,440
where Goo comes out, where Sup is

388
00:24:56,980 --> 00:24:58,820
Well, village lane, village lane

389
00:24:58,820 --> 00:25:00,280
Paipo paipo paipo no

390
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:02,320
Shūringan, Shūringan no

391
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:04,440
Gūrindai, Gūrindai no

392
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:06,340
Ponpopokī no, Ponpokonā no

393
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:07,940
Chōsuke of the ultimate name

394
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:16,100
Uhahaha!

395
00:25:16,340 --> 00:25:18,500
The Chief started dancing?!

396
00:25:19,580 --> 00:25:21,580
Doesn't suit you! What, a temple taro?

397
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:22,620
Hyahahaha!

398
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:24,340
Volvo and Sahonji too?

399
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:25,400
Nyagyahahaha!

400
00:25:25,520 --> 00:25:27,320
Hey, wait!
Hold on, something's going on here!

401
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:29,340
Alright! I'm joining in too!

402
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:32,600
Next time, Dance Dance Dance! See you then!

403
00:25:33,780 --> 00:25:35,920
That place is Kameary,

404
00:25:37,180 --> 00:25:39,540
surely Kameary,

405
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:44,280
everybody come on over to our town!

406
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:45,840
Thank you!

